`ReactDOM.unmountComponentAtNode` has been removed in React 19. Use `root.unmount()` instead.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE (React 18 and earlier)
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom';
ReactDOM.unmountComponentAtNode(container);

// ✅ AFTER (React 19)
root.unmount();
```
</details>

`ReactDOM.findDOMNode` has been removed in React 19. Use DOM `ref` instead.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE
const node = ReactDOM.findDOMNode(this);

// ✅ AFTER
const nodeRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
return <div ref={nodeRef} />;
```
</details>

`React.PropTypes` is removed in React 19. Use TypeScript types or the `prop-types` package.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE
MyComponent.propTypes = {
  title: React.PropTypes.string
};

// ✅ AFTER
import PropTypes from 'prop-types';
MyComponent.propTypes = {
  title: PropTypes.string
};
```
</details>

String refs are removed in React 19. Use `useRef()` or callback refs.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE
<input ref="nameInput" />

// ✅ AFTER
const inputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);
<input ref={inputRef} />
```
</details>

Legacy lifecycle methods like `componentWillReceiveProps` are removed in React 19.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE
componentWillReceiveProps(nextProps) {
  this.setState({ count: nextProps.count });
}

// ✅ AFTER (componentDidUpdate or Hooks)
componentDidUpdate(prevProps) {
  if (prevProps.count !== this.props.count) {
    this.setState({ count: this.props.count });
  }
}
```
</details>

`useFormState` is deprecated in React 19. Use `useActionState` from `'react'`.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE
import { useFormState } from 'react-dom';
const [state, formAction] = useFormState(action, initialState);

// ✅ AFTER
import { useActionState } from 'react';
const [state, formAction, isPending] = useActionState(action, initialState);
```
</details>

`react-dom/test-utils` is deprecated in React 19. Import `act` directly from `'react'`.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE
import { act } from 'react-dom/test-utils';

// ✅ AFTER
import { act } from 'react';
```
</details>
